Everyone these days delights seeing knights in armor;
and since these brutes are allegorical,
they'll just likely manage to please all the more.

The horizon has gone dark;
here and there an ominous red flash;
the bloody flare of weapons;
everything now joins in:
rocks, forest, air, even the heavens.

These honors as bestowed are sacred and valid;
and yet, for confirmation, we will put it to paper.
And here I see coming just the man to do that.

Then feel it now in my parting curse!
Mankind is blind from birth;
you, Faustus, are blind now at your last!
